   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the city of Syracuse and the board of education of the city\nschool district of the city of Syracuse cooperative school reconstruction act,\nin relation to construction and design contracts entered into by the JSC Board",
    "basePrintNo": "S6209",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6209-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part A-4 §5, Chap 58 of 2006",
    "lawSection": "Syracuse, City of",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6209\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the city of Syracuse and the board of education of the\ncity school district of the city of Syracuse cooperative school recon-\nstruction act, in relation to construction and design contracts entered\ninto by the JSC Board\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation increases the maximum bonding limit for Phase III of\nthe Syracuse Joint Schools Construction Board from $300 to $400 million.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: increases the maximum bonding limit for Phase III of the\nSyracuse Joint Schools Construction Board from $300 to $400 million.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 2021 with Chapter 617 the Legislature authorized a third phase of\nrenovations for Syracuse City School buildings through the Joint Schools\nConstruction Board. It originally authorized up to $300 million in bond-\ning. However, due to inflation and other external factors, construction\ncosts have risen sharply. Authorizing an additional $100 million in\nbonding will ensure the Joint Schools Construction Board can finish\nplanned Phase III projects and provide Syracuse City School students\nwith up to date facilities.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill, amending chapter 617 of 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
